# Old Man of the Sea holds what it took "for as long as ... that creature's power remains less than or equal to this creature's
# power" (CR 611.2b); "if it stops being a creature, its power is considered to be 0" (its ruling). Bot1's Old Man (2/3) takes
# Bot2's Llanowar Elves. Bot2 makes the Elves a Vehicle artifact with Swift Reconfiguration: no creature, no power (CR 208.3),
# counted as 0 - no more than Old Man's 2, so Bot1 keeps it. Bot2 then casts Ray of Enfeeblement on Old Man (blue, so -4/-1):
# a -2/2, and 0 is greater than -2, so the effect ends at once and the Elves goes back to Bot2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Old Man of the Sea
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Swift Reconfiguration
Ray of Enfeeblement
Forest x14

